; The bid as a signal (C4; p. 89, the partner's bid the only information
; before play): does the bidder hold two doubles or more? Asked from another
; seat, the hand's own auction read as evidence (README, The auction as
; evidence):
;
;   silas query examples/book/bidding/bidder-holds-two-doubles.silas \
;     --hand hand-29 --seat partner --auction 30,pass,pass,pass \
;     --read bidder=examples/book/bidding/bid-only-enough.silas \
;     --offered P6,P5,P4,P3,P2,P1,P0
;
; Hand 29 (fours, 30), the partner at trick one: the uniform deal and the
; bidder's 30 and fours read as bid-only-enough makes them
; (tests/book_auction.rs has the partner's numbers before the lead, and
; tests/cli.rs this one's).
(include book)

(query
  (declarer b)
  (<= 2 (card (roles d) (double d) (holds b d))))
